# The generated SFX stay out of git: ElevenLabs' Prohibited Use Policy (17 Aug 2026) bars distributing
# Sound Effects output "on a standalone basis ... as isolated files, audio samples, ... libraries, or
# other collections of sounds". They live on disk for mix.py; the finished soundtrack (mix.m4a/mix.wav),
# cues.json, sfx/library.json (prompts) and the scripts are tracked. See short/sources.md, "Asset licenses".
# Delete this rule only if the repo stays private to the account owner.
sfx/*.wav
__pycache__/
# The music is licensed for use in the video, but the Eleven Music terms prohibit putting it in "Music Libraries &
# Repositories", and this repo is public. So the standalone music and the soundtrack stems stay out of git too;
# the published video carries them. The plan, cues and scripts are tracked.
music.wav
src/*.mp3
mix.wav
mix.m4a
